// Energy Research Warehouse (ERW) site, session 1404 (chain 100): the Grid tool's panels, rendered, held to their keys,
// their words and their held lines. Without a build, a server or a request leaving this machine.
//
//   node --import ./scripts/alias-register.mjs --import ./scripts/tsx-register.mjs scripts/test-grid-render.mjs
//
// Many tests/test_session*.py pin the Grid tool's source word for word (a line of markup, a key's template, a sentence
// in a component). This test checks the same things where a reader meets them: on the page as the server draws it.
// The page (app/grid/page.tsx) is called as it is and walked as Next renders it on the server, on the committed real rows
// of scripts/test-grid-files.mjs and test-grid-failed-reads.mjs, through scripts/grid-render-standin.mjs (the stand-in for
// PostgREST and Storage, the walk, the clock at the fixtures' read time; two fixtures more for the older blocks the pins
// read: the battery units of session 1180 and ERCOT's day of session 1166). One case a panel and a kind of grid: an ISO
// with prices (ERCOT), CAISO, a held grid (ISO-NE; MISO on the Clean tab, where the fixture holds its week and its
// committed clean figures are held), the Lower 48, and PJM (no price held) where a panel says so; and the older blocks a
// pinned test reads, where the fixtures draw them. For each case:
//   panel     the block is drawn on its page under its name (data-grid-panel, or the attribute that names it) and no
//             component in it threw
//   keys      its own figures (each distinct data-check key) are `figures` in number, by kind (`kinds`: the key's first
//             part, or fmt and the kind it formats), and every figure carries its value (data-raw); each of `keys` (a
//             key's template up to its first value, as a pinned test reads it in the source) starts a figure of the block
//   words     each of `words` is in its rendered words or in the words on hover (a title, a reason, a chart's name), as a
//             reader reads them (entities read, every run of space one space): the sentences the pins hold, its headings
//   held      a held grid's block says "license needed" and why (`held`, the reasons on hover), and draws no figure of
//             the held table (its `kinds`)
//   anchor    each of `anchors` is an id of the block, or of the element that holds it alone (lib/gridAnchors.ts)
//   method    each of `methods` (a METHOD_ constant of lib/gridAnchors.ts, or a note's address) is a link of the block
//   files     the block offers exactly `files` (components/grid/PanelFile.tsx, data-grid-file)
//   order     (session 1405, where a case gives it) each of `order` is in its rendered words, each after the one before:
//             the Ask column's stored answers, the tab on screen's first (lib/gridask.ts orderByTab)
// And: every panel family drawn on these pages (grid_<panel>_) has a case, so a panel added later fails here until it
// has one. A pinned python assertion this test covers carries the line
//   # also covered by site/scripts/test-grid-render.mjs: <case name>
// above it (tests/test_session1404.py holds each such line to a case of this file); the assertion itself is kept, to be
// retired only with the owner's leave.
// Session 1406 (chain 100): the Lower 48's Network case draws the seven grids' demand and the Lower 48's, and the seven's
// exchange in words (components/grid/Lower48Demand.tsx); and the stand-in now reads the week's generation and demand of
// fixtures/grid_balance.json as the [ts_utc, value] rows the fixture holds (it had read each row as a value, so six
// grids' demand and generation were NaN): the balance of CAISO and ISO-NE gains its week, the gravity table its shares.
// A figure whose value is NaN is a figure without a value.
// Session 1412 (chain 107): the Flex Alert scorecard (/grid/caiso/alerts, its own page file) has a case, its small charts
